  "slug": "cortical-eeg-2098",
  "summary": "Three April 2026 preprints present open-source analysis tools and an errors-in-variables reanalysis of ABIDE-I confound estimation.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the construction and correction of analysis pipelines for human neuroimaging, where analytic choices directly shape reported effects. MLE-Toolbox packages end-to-end EEG and MEG workflows in an open-source MATLAB GUI, spanning preprocessing, source localization, connectivity, phase-amplitude coupling, and machine learning. BrainPET Studio offers an open-source desktop GUI for atlas-based regional PET quantification in MNI space that avoids FreeSurfer and is validated against ADNI. The IQ-Motion preprint is a different kind of contribution: it applies an errors-in-variables estimator to ABIDE-I and suggests that pooled OLS overstates the IQ-motion slope in autism fMRI confound correction, framing the inflation as potentially driven by site-correlated measurement uncertainty. What is new across the set is explicit attention to estimator bias and accessible, reproducible tooling, rather than a shared modality or mechanistic finding, since the items differ in modality and aim.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-04-14"
}
